<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cathedral of the Holy Cross, Aghtamar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">915–921</span> · Also known as Church of the Holy Cross</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cathedral of the Holy Cross on Aghtamar island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a> was built between 915 and 921 by the architect Manuel for King Gagik I Artsruni of Vaspurakan. Its outer walls are covered with relief carvings of biblical scenes, the king and animals, making it a masterpiece of medieval Armenian art. It later served as seat of the Catholicos of Aghtamar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cathedral-of-the-holy-cross-aghtamar.jpg" alt="Cathedral of the Holy Cross, Aghtamar" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bini · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geva%C5%9F,_isola_di_akdamar,_chiesa_armena_della_santa_croce,_x_secolo,_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
